&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;⚡️&lt;/span&gt; &lt;span style="text-transform: uppercase;    font-weight: 600; font-size: 1.2em;"&gt;IN BRIEF&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⚙️ &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/181164/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;The first beta of WordPress 7.0&lt;/a&gt; is now available. The big focus is the addition of real-time collaboration.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;⬆️ &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/181217/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;The Navigation API is now Baseline Newly Available&lt;/a&gt; across all major browsers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;😮 Someone has created an &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/181165/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;x86 emulator in CSS&lt;/a&gt;, no JS! You'll need to open it in a Chromium-based browser.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;🔶 Zach has had a go at &lt;a href="https://frontendfoc.us/link/181166/rss" style=" color: #D94306; font-weight: 600;"&gt;creating a logo for HTML&lt;/a&gt;. The old orange shield for HTML 5 was likely the closest we've gotten to an 'official' logo for the language.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;/td&gt;&lt;/tr&gt;&lt;/table&gt;
